# ==============================================================================
# GeckoPod-ModZ: CrossLink-NX LIFCL-17 QFN72 Physical Constraints
# Target: LIFCL-17 QFN72
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - This file intentionally does NOT contain guessed package-site assignments.
#   - Populate ldc_set_location only after checking the official LIFCL-17 pinout
#     (FPGA-SC-02006) and the QFN72 package/migration documentation.
#   - Keep timing constraints in the companion .sdc file.
# ==============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Electrical standards
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The iPod LCD bus is expected to be ~1.8 V logic. Confirm the selected bank's
# VCCIO is actually powered at 1.8 V before enabling direct connection.

ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18} [get_ports clk_sys]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP} [get_ports rst_n]

ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP}   [get_ports ipod_wr_n]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP}   [get_ports ipod_cs_n]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=DOWN} [get_ports ipod_rs]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP}   [get_ports ipod_reset_n]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=DOWN} [get_ports {ipod_db[*]}]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Package locations -- TODO before PCB freeze
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do not assign sequential QFN package numbers by assumption. The QFN contains
# power/configuration/D-PHY pins and bank restrictions; arbitrary numbering can
# collide with non-user pins or split the 16-bit bus across unsuitable banks.
#
# Preferred placement goals:
#   1. Put ipod_db[15:0] and control signals in 1.8-V-capable user-I/O banks.
#   2. Keep the 16-bit input bus physically compact for routing.
#   3. Preserve the hardened D-PHY pins required by the AMOLED output.
#   4. Put clk_sys on a clock-capable input.
#   5. Reserve programming/configuration/JTAG pins and required power pins.
#
# Example syntax once verified:
# ldc_set_location -site {<OFFICIAL_SITE>} [get_ports ipod_wr_n]
# ldc_set_location -site {<OFFICIAL_SITE>} [get_ports {ipod_db[0]}]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Notes
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The current RTL is controller-agnostic and should use the ipod_bus_capture
# top-level naming rather than the earlier ipod_s1d19122_capture assumption.
